hard:
adj. dispassionate;
adj. resisting weight or pressure
adj. very strong or vigorous

hardest:
adj. not easy; requiring great physical or mental effort to accomplish or comprehend or endure
adj. dispassionate;
adj. resisting weight or pressure

heaves:
n. A disease of horses, characterized by difficult breathing,
with heaving of the flank, wheezing, flatulency, and a peculiar cough;
broken wind.

hell:
n. any place of pain and turmoil;
n. a cause of difficulty and suffering
n. (Christianity) the abode of Satan and the forces of evil; where sinners suffer eternal punishment

his:
pron. Belonging or pertaining to him; -- used as a pronominal
adjective or adjective pronoun; as, tell John his papers are ready;
formerly used also for its, but this use is now obsolete.
